
  <sn><md>### Biomagnification

**Biomagnification** is the **increase in the concentration of a persistent chemical pollutant at successive trophic levels of a food chain**.
In simple terms, a pollutant becomes **more concentrated as it moves from lower organisms to higher organisms through feeding**.

![img](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Nh-emon/QDoc/main/SES3/Enviromental%20Pollution%20and%20Mitigation/02.Key%20Definitions/assets/biomagnification_diagram.jpeg)


+++ **Basic food-chain pattern**

```text
Polluted water
      ↓
Phytoplankton
      ↓
Zooplankton
      ↓
Small fish
      ↓
Large fish
      ↓
Fish-eating bird / Human
```

The concentration of the pollutant generally increases upward:

```text
Water
  ↓
Phytoplankton       → low concentration
  ↓
Zooplankton         → higher
  ↓
Small fish          → higher
  ↓
Large fish          → much higher
  ↓
Top predator        → highest concentration
```

+++
